`EventTicket` gains indexes on `created` and `closed_at`. Neither was indexed, and both carry the range scans the ticket-flow queries make. This is the whole of the schema Phase 5B adds - the phase introduces no model and no counter.

The app now ships one page template, and [ADR 0008](../docs/decisions/0008-ui-component-framework-only.md) carries an amendment saying why. Nautobot's UI Component Framework renders panels inside an object detail page, and core ships no template that takes a bare list of panels, so a dashboard with no object behind it needs a file of its own. It extends `base.html` alone and its body is three calls to the framework's own `render_components` tag. `TemplateGuardTest` changes from a flat prohibition to a one-file allowlist and additionally asserts that the allowed file extends nothing but the base, which is the coupling the ADR was actually about.
